# Editors and operating systems
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local demo material: generated keys, certificates, passwords and secret files.
# Generators are committed (scripts/generate_demo_material.py); their output never is.
.demo/

# Shop-pilot material: the same rule, for a real shop rather than a demo. These are live
# credentials for a running business -- database passwords, a TLS private key, the Keycloak
# bootstrap admin -- so the directory is ignored before it exists rather than after.
.shop/

# Adversarial-review scratch tests. A verifier writes a throwaway probe file, runs it, and deletes
# it; the review instructions say so in as many words ("a scratch test you delete afterwards").
# Three times during RANGE-PRICE-001 and PROMO-WIRING-001 one of those files existed at the moment
# a `git add -A` ran, and once it reached a commit -- 504 lines whose own docstring said "Deleted
# after the review", which made two of that item's acceptance_checks fail on a clean checkout while
# passing for everyone who already had the file deleted locally.
#
# Ignoring the name is the durable fix: a reviewer's probe can no longer be committed by accident,
# and a probe worth keeping has to be renamed to something that says what it proves, which is the
# rename it deserved anyway.
test_zz_*.py
*_scratch.py
*_scratch_*.py
